# __APP_NAME__

A Next.js app that runs [ShipProbe](https://github.com/kyisaiah47/shipprobe) checks on its own
server. It was scaffolded with `shipprobe --app __MODE__`.

```sh
npm install
npm run dev
```

The app runs three checks:

- a security scan of a deployed URL, which needs the visitor to confirm they own the app or are
  authorised to scan it;
- an install-time check of an npm package;
- a score for a pasted AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md or similar file.

Page, plan and promote checks need a browser or a repository on disk, so they run from the CLI:
`npx shipprobe page <url>`.

The security route refuses literal private and loopback addresses. Set
`SHIPPROBE_ALLOW_PRIVATE=1` to scan a host on your own network. A public hostname that resolves
to a private address is not caught by that check, so run a public deployment behind an egress
proxy if that matters to you.
